Map permanent popups as xdg_popups on webOS.

Firefox keeps noautohide panels (the add-on install prompt, among others)
out of its popup hierarchy and gives them GDK_WINDOW_TYPE_HINT_UTILITY,
which GTK maps as a plain wl_subsurface. The webOS compositor never shows
those, so the prompt stayed invisible and add-ons could not be installed
from addons.mozilla.org. Give them the popup-menu hint instead: GTK then
maps them as xdg_popups, which the webOS adapter shows as its own
subsurfaces and never dismisses on outside clicks. They stay untracked, as
upstream; tracking them instead made Firefox close them at once, since
they are not in layout's popup list.

reverted
diff --git a/widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp b/widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp
index 69ae6a6c20..091c9286e3 100644
--- a/widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp
+++ b/widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp
@@ -1453,10 +1453,13 @@ bool nsWindowWayland::WaylandPopupConfigure() {
   }
 
   if (!mPopupTrackInHierarchy) {
-    // GDK_WINDOW_TYPE_HINT_UTILITY is mapped as wl_subsurface
-    // by default.
-    LOG("  not tracked in popup hierarchy, switch to Utility");
-    gtkTypeHint = GDK_WINDOW_TYPE_HINT_UTILITY;
+    // webOS: GDK maps GDK_WINDOW_TYPE_HINT_UTILITY as a plain wl_subsurface,
+    // which the webOS compositor never displays (the add-on install prompt
+    // stayed invisible). Map untracked (permanent) popups as xdg_popups
+    // instead; the webOS adapter shows those and never dismisses them on
+    // outside clicks. They stay out of the popup hierarchy, as upstream.
+    LOG("  not tracked in popup hierarchy, map as xdg_popup (webOS)");
+    gtkTypeHint = GDK_WINDOW_TYPE_HINT_POPUP_MENU;
   }
   gtk_window_set_type_hint(GTK_WINDOW(mShell), gtkTypeHint);
 
